(7237102, 1111441, 69008, '<td valign="top">The color of the bird blending into the color of the water behind it may have dinged this one in voting.  <br/>For wildlife, it''s usually better if you can crop to have the critter "coming into" the image with room to go forward.<br/>You captured a great pose, from a good angle,and did a nicely artistic rendering of the subject as well.</td>', 'The color of the bird blending into the color of the water behind it may have dinged this one in voting.  For wildlife, it''s usually better if you can crop to have the critter "coming into" the image with room to go forward.You captured a great pose, from a good angle,and did a nicely artistic rendering of the subject as well.', '2014-07-06 00:04:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7238874, 1110741, 98339, '<td valign="top">3 questions...<br/> <br/>Did you use a tri-pod.<br/> <br/>And did you use a trigger to take the picture (vs hitting the shutter button yourself).<br/> <br/>And was your VR turned off.<br/> <br/>You have the slightest of movement in the capture...otherwise this could really be a stunning shot.<br/> <br/>You must live close to Downtown...</td>', '3 questions... Did you use a tri-pod. And did you use a trigger to take the picture (vs hitting the shutter button yourself). And was your VR turned off. You have the slightest of movement in the capture...otherwise this could really be a stunning shot. You must live close to Downtown...', '2014-07-08 20:55:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7238949, 1110741, 50189, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Ja-9:</b></div><hr/><i> 3 questions...<br/> <br/>Did you use a tri-pod.<br/> <br/>And did you use a trigger to take the picture (vs hitting the shutter button yourself).<br/> <br/>And was your VR turned off.<br/> <br/>You have the slightest of movement in the capture...otherwise this could really be a stunning shot.<br/> <br/>You must live close to Downtown... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I did use a tri-pod and a wired trigger, I do admit I am not sure what VR is though.   I work near downtown and was passing through.  It was a picture that I had been wanting to take, and I thought that the night was right for it.  This was my first attempt at night photography.  I was pretty happy with it.  Now if I could do as well on my others.  I am not sure if I need to upgrade lenses or if my issues are more on the processing area.  I have been trying to figure out what lens to get next.</td>', 'Originally posted by Ja-9: 3 questions... Did you use a tri-pod. And did you use a trigger to take the picture (vs hitting the shutter button yourself). And was your VR turned off. You have the slightest of movement in the capture...otherwise this could really be a stunning shot. You must live close to Downtown...   I did use a tri-pod and a wired trigger, I do admit I am not sure what VR is though.   I work near downtown and was passing through.  It was a picture that I had been wanting to take, and I thought that the night was right for it.  This was my first attempt at night photography.  I was pretty happy with it.  Now if I could do as well on my others.  I am not sure if I need to upgrade lenses or if my issues are more on the processing area.  I have been trying to figure out what lens to get next.', '2014-07-08 23:14:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7255892, 1109741, 50695, '<td valign="top">this shows that you like a "busy" composition with no single focus, and you''re not afraid of competing colors. I like that, too.</td>', 'this shows that you like a "busy" composition with no single focus, and you''re not afraid of competing colors. I like that, too.', '2014-08-27 13:50:14.000000', NULL, 0),
